  "reason": "Ticket sender reports a suspicious email from 'IT Support' asking for her password. Checking account status before handling the report per KB-008."
}

{
  "email": "hannah.lee@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Per KB-008 quick check: see whether similar password-request messages were caught in the sender's mailbox quarantine."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Thank you for reporting this, Hannah, and for not replying. IT Support will not ask you for your password by email, so please treat that message as a phishing attempt. Please don't click any links, reply to it, or forward it to colleagues. Leave it in your mailbox for now so the security team can examine it. A member of the security team will look into the sender and block it if needed. If you do end up clicking a link or entering your password anywhere, let us know right away.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket EVAL-sec-06. Sender Hannah Lee (user_id 12, Finance, Payroll Specialist, active, not VIP, sign-in not blocked, failed logins 0, must_change_password already set). The user reports an email from 'IT Support' asking for her password to finish account setup. She did not reply, so KB-029 does not apply. Quarantine for her mailbox is empty, so there are no similar caught messages. Per KB-008, a reported suspicious email is always escalated so a person can review the sender and block it for everyone if needed. Sender address and exact subject were not included in the ticket, so Tier 2 should get them from the user's mailbox. Also check whether other Finance users received the same message. No release, reset, or block actions were taken. Note that must_change_password is set and password_last_set is 2026-10-11; confirm whether this relates to a genuine onboarding step and whether the 'IT Support' email is a lure.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
